## Build page layout fix (Lakebase)

### Context
The PR#47 merge changed `_renderEngineUi` to actively remove `d-none` from `dtLakebaseBuildNote` for Lakebase engine. The build note element carries Bootstrap's `w-100` class (intended to push it below the architecture cards). However, `.dt-arch-lakebase-section` was a flex container without `flex-wrap`, so the 100%-wide note could not wrap and instead squashed the Triple Store → Sync → Graph DB card row.

### Changes
1. `src/front/static/query/css/query-sync.css` — Added `flex-wrap: wrap` to `.dt-arch-lakebase-section:not(.d-none)` so the `w-100` build note wraps below the three arch cards as intended.

### Modified files
- `src/front/static/query/css/query-sync.css`

### Test results
No unit tests cover CSS layout; visual fix verified via code inspection.
